{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1162374-does-soulless-affect-spellcasting","id":1162374,"title":"Does Soulless affect spellcasting?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-25T00:12:53-08:00","id":1162374,"title":"Does Soulless affect spellcasting?","content":"Does the Soulless Condition inhibit spellcasting on a mage? It doesn't seem to be the case RAW because only the Thrall Condition mentions that mages cannot cast spells. However, if souls are what enables spellcasting to begin with and you don't have one it seems to me like Soulless should equally inhibit spellcasting or at least impose difficulties on casting spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T00:20:13-08:00","id":1162376,"title":"","content":"IIRC you automatically cause Paradox, but you can still cast spells. Your soul is a different thing from your Gnosis, which is also why you don't lose your Legacy if you get souljacked and replace it with a new one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T00:22:00-08:00","id":1162377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1162374-does-soulless-affect-spellcasting#post1162374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the Soulless Condition inhibit spellcasting on a mage? It doesn't seem to be the case RAW because only the Thrall Condition mentions that mages cannot cast spells. However, if souls are what enables spellcasting to begin with and you don't have one it seems to me like Soulless should equally inhibit spellcasting or at least impose difficulties on casting spells.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You are correct only thrall inhibits mages casting spells. However soulless makes all spellcasting risk paradox as per p98. A soul is needed for healthy spellcasting but the ability to cast without one means its not needed. Think of it like a bath plug, its important to have one to take a bath but when you remove it you can keep having a bath until the water runs out. (ie willpower or gnosis to get to thrall)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T00:54:16-08:00","id":1162380,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your answers! I only read the text for Conditions which did not have the information I was looking for.<br /> <br /> So if Soulless imposes automatic Paradox and Thrall stops spellcasting entirely, what does Enervated mean as a middle step between the two? I'm thinking of automatic Paradox and +2 dice to the Paradox roll for Enervated characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T03:30:28-08:00","id":1162415,"title":"","content":"I think enerveted in itself is bad enough, and Soul loss already gives +1 die on all paradox, you can't hold it in and all paradox rolls have the Rote quality. It's bound to be some shit if the mage actually uses magic. And all spells are paradox risks. Which means, every spell gives another die to the paradox pool if it's in the same scene. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}